                    A graph with 10 vertices labeled 0 to 9. For the vertices with labels 0 through 4, the vertex with label <m>i</m> has neighbors <m>i-1</m>, <m>i+1</m>, and <m>i+5</m>. The first two adjacencies are interpreted cyclically so that, for instance, <m>4</m> has neighbors <m>3</m> and <m>0</m>. For the vertices with labels 5 through 9, the vertex with label <m>i</m> has neighbors <m>i-5</m>, <m>i+2</m>, and <m>i+3</m>. The second and third adjacencies are interpreted cyclically so that, for instance, <m>9</m> has neighbors <m>6</m> and <m>7</m>. There is also an edge between the vertices with labels <m>7</m> and <m>8</m>.
                  </p>
